  "notes": "NaN (decision D-046 (4)): the quantity coords holds 2070 NaN values in 444 samples (mode 1: 146, mode 5: 1, mode 7: 297; mode 1 = one scale 2^-500..2^500 per sample, mode 5 = sliver triangles, mode 7 = 1e+-150 scaling). They are oracle behaviour: CGAL's Simple_cartesian<double> construction of the intersection point (Line_3/Plane_3 and Segment_3/Triangle_3 formulas, no overflow check) overflows to +-inf on these magnitudes and then evaluates inf - inf, inf / inf or 0 * inf; the port evaluates the same operations. The NaN is the platform's default NaN (x86_64: 0xfff8000000000000, aarch64: 0x7ff8000000000000); no other quantity and no input contains NaN."
